# Samsung Galaxy A21s (Exynos850) Mainline

This manifest provides all the repositories and tools needed to compile
and boot mainline Linux on your Galaxy A21s.

**NOTE: This guide is ONLY for installing the kernel, to install a Linux
Operating System, Post Market OS should be used.**

To initialize the source code, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/samsungexynos850/manifest.git -b master
```
Then to sync up
```
repo sync
```

Compilation
-----------

This guide assumes you already have LLVM installed on your x86_64 host
and all other dependencies needed to compile Linux.

Run this command to start compilation:
```
./build.sh
```

Installation
------------

Install the flashable boot image using a custom recovery that provides a
fastboot daemon (LineageOS recovery is recommended)

Once in recovery mode enter fastboot mode and run the following command.
```
fastboot flash boot out/images/boot.img
```
